{
 "title": "Windows won't let you name a folder CON",
 "captions": [
  {
   "text": "Windows won't let you name a folder !CON.!",
   "say": "Windows won't let you name a folder con.",
   "hide": true
  },
  {
   "text": "Try it, and Windows says the device name is !invalid.!"
  },
  {
   "text": "Device? The reason is *older than folders.*"
  },
  {
   "text": "In early DOS, *CON* meant the console: your keyboard and screen.",
   "say": "In early DOS, con meant the console: your keyboard and screen."
  },
  {
   "text": "*PRN* was the printer. !NUL! threw everything away.",
   "say": "P R N was the printer. Null threw everything away."
  },
  {
   "text": "Programs used these names like *files* to talk to hardware."
  },
  {
   "text": "When DOS added folders in *1983,* the names had to work in !every folder.!",
   "say": "When DOS added folders in nineteen eighty-three, the names had to work in every folder."
  },
  {
   "text": "So Microsoft reserved them !everywhere.!"
  },
  {
   "text": "Over forty years later, Windows still blocks them, for hardware from the *eighties.*"
  }
 ],
